\section{Administrator Capability Model}
The current backend authority object contains five explicit booleans: \texttt{manageAssessmentForms}, \texttt{manageCarousel}, \texttt{manageAttendance}, \texttt{manageArchives}, and \texttt{manageNextGenQa}. Chief administrators receive the full authority set. A non-Chief administrator must be active and hold the specific capability for backend-protected operations that implement capability checks.

\section{Pastor Authorization}
Pastor access is not a database role lookup. The Worker currently uses a case-insensitive anchored email allowlist matching \texttt{rev.ibrahim@lincministry.com}. The browser calls the backend session/access endpoint through \texttt{usePastorAccess}; protected routes use the returned Pastor state. Sensitive Pastor APIs independently enforce the same server-side rule after Firebase ID-token verification.
