\section{Recommended Capability Expansion}
Capabilities should map to server actions, not page visibility. The capability namespace proposed earlier in this chapter can be extended with read/write distinctions when ministry governance needs them, for example \texttt{nextgen.files.read} versus \texttt{nextgen.files.manage}, or \texttt{attendance.read} versus \texttt{attendance.correct}. A technical administrator should not automatically gain confidential pastoral data merely because that administrator can configure public content.

\section{Non-Delegable or Highly Restricted Actions}
Unless ministry leadership explicitly decides otherwise, Pastor meeting-request decisions, highly confidential People Notes, pastoral/member care notes, and other ministry judgments should not be automatically inherited by Chief or general technical administration. Database/production operators may possess emergency infrastructure access, but that privilege should be documented, exceptional, and audited rather than represented as ordinary application authorization.

