This list is an important migration checklist: a domain is not fully behind the backend while its sensitive persistence still depends on direct browser database access.
\chapter{Maintenance Checklist}
\begin{enumerate}
\item Update this document whenever a route is added/removed, a database root changes, a capability is added, an external provider changes, or an authorization boundary changes.
\item Keep backend README authorization statements synchronized with route middleware.
\item Treat \nolinkurl{documentation/database/*.mmd} as versioned schema documentation and update it with migrations.
\item Add new public/backend endpoints to the API matrix and test catalog in the same release.
\item Record new environment variables in both deployment configuration and this catalog; never put secret values in documentation.
\item When a direct-Firebase domain migrates to Hono, remove it from the residual-client appendix only after source imports and runtime flow are both gone.
\item Remove legacy modules only after verifying no route, barrel export, migration routine, or production data still depends on them.
\end{enumerate}

